{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And He chose his seed after him.</b> An allusion to Jacob. For had it said 'their seed after them,' there would be an opening for the eight nations that came from Abraham and from Isaac besides us, to say: we are chosen like you." "<b>And He brought you out before Him.</b> Before the Egyptians, as it goes on to explain, as it is written: 'all the hosts of YHWH went out לעיני מצרים' (before the Egyptians). And we find that Egyptians are called in singular language: 'and here מצרים (Egypt) pursues them.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:42.776303912Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}